INT. INFLATABLE CASTLE RENTAL SHOP - DAY

A warehouse full of deflated bouncy castles, piled like sleeping dragons. Fans hum. A cash register dings.

MAURICE "MO" DELACROIX-BROWN (50s, polo shirt, sunburnt nose) stands behind the counter. Across from him, bride-to-be PAIGE QUINTANILLA (30s, tailored blazer, manic energy) taps a tablet. Behind her, her mother GLADYS QUINTANILLA (60s, enormous sunglasses) examines a banner. In the corner, a lanky teenager, FITZ (17, apron with a name tag), pumps a foot blower.

PAIGE
It has to be a castle. Not a bouncy house. A castle.

MO
Ma'am, they're the same thing.

PAIGE
They are not the same thing.

MO
It has turrets. It bounces.

PAIGE
My wedding is in six days.

Mo takes a long breath. Gladys tilts her sunglasses down.

GLADYS
Paige, honey, nobody's going to bounce at a wedding.

PAIGE
Mom, there are twelve children coming.

GLADYS
Twelve children and nobody's bouncing.

Fitz stops pumping. The blower wheezes out. He looks at the others and says nothing.

MO
I have the Camelot Deluxe. Seven by seven. Cannons on the parapet.

PAIGE
How many cannons?

MO
Four.

PAIGE
Do they fire?

MO
Air, ma'am.

PAIGE
Fire real things?

MO
Absolutely not.

Paige narrows her eyes. Gladys lowers her sunglasses all the way and stares at Mo, then at the ceiling, as if praying.

PAIGE
I'll take the Camelot.

MO
Wonderful.

PAIGE
But I want it in pink.

MO
It's gray.

PAIGE
Make it pink.

Mo looks at Fitz. Fitz looks at the floor. The register dings by itself.

MO
Fitz. Do we own pink paint?

FITZ
We own a lot of paint.

MO
Pink?

FITZ
There's some salmon.

MO
Salmon is pink.

PAIGE
It is not.

GLADYS
Paige, salmon is a lovely color.

PAIGE
Mother!

Gladys folds her arms. Paige breathes through her nose. Mo slides a clipboard across the counter, and Paige signs without reading. Fitz resumes pumping, a little faster than before.

MO
Six days, then. I'll deliver Friday morning.

PAIGE
Thursday night.

MO
Friday morning.

PAIGE
Thursday.

MO
(to himself)
Thursday it is.

Paige sweeps out. Gladys lingers, takes off the sunglasses, and slips Mo a folded fifty.

GLADYS
For your trouble.

She puts the glasses back on and follows her daughter out the door.

FITZ
Was that a tip?

MO
That was a ransom.
